 & 2 & -9 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/state.json" "file_sha256" "bad8bf355a2d98eb4d09c16da2e9a1b14334a08a175647bfc8ad054277c71a4e" "basis" 1462 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to get the minor of ${d}_{15}$, we remove the $1$st row and $5$th column: \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 & ∗ \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{15}=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${d}_{15}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{15} & =(-1)^{1+5}{M}_{15} \\\\  & ={M}_{15} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/state.json" "file_sha256" "bad8bf355a2d98eb4d09c16da2e9a1b14334a08a175647bfc8ad054277c71a4e" "basis" 1462 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32793" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039717/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "079affb9679cf342141ab56f4aba9a7e48b2be1c797f70d41c4e589f5b75d13c" "basis" 1462 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha